            <div xml:id="d1250">

                <pb facs="1479" n="1281" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/7–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1250<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The White House Map Room to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg?</hi></placeName>], <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-25">25 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>313. The President requests an immediate answer to White House message #311
                        (241035Z).<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1250-f1"/> If an answer is not received
                    within twenty-four hours, the proclamation will be released by the President and
                    the Prime Minister. Please advise time of receipt of this message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
